# Fallback on-screen keyboard (task 014 P2b) on the native Settings' development page System > Keyboard test, with
# APPLAUNCH_OSK=force (the harness has no presence watcher; on a board the keyboard shows only when no physical
# keyboard is present). The keys are tapped through the touch path (tapkey). Shots: the System section with
# "On-screen keyboard: Auto", the Text field editing with the letters page, Shift armed, the 123 page, Ctrl armed, the
# Number field on the number pad, the Password field masked. Review only: no golden; the page header is checked against the
# home grid's (run.sh header).
title on-screen keyboard
review
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 1
env APPLAUNCH_OSK force
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
header home
launch Settings
# System is the last section (Up wraps there); in it, from the end: Shutdown, Reboot, Keyboard test, On-screen keyboard
key UP
key ENTER
key UP
key UP
key UP
key UP
shot osk_setting
key DOWN
key ENTER
# the Text field edits at once: letters page
tapkey h
tapkey i
shot osk_letters
# the page title is "Key test" (the row "Keyboard test": the title fits whole left of the strip's reserved SSH slot)
header osk_letters "Settings > System > Key test" "System > Key test" "Key test"
tapkey SHIFT
shot osk_shift
tapkey A
tapkey 123
shot osk_123
tapkey abc
tapkey Ctrl
shot osk_ctrl
tapkey Ctrl
# Tab: the next field (Number) and its number pad
tapkey Tab
tapkey 4
tapkey 2
shot osk_numpad
tapkey Tab
tapkey s
tapkey e
tapkey c
tapkey r
tapkey e
tapkey t
shot osk_password
# Esc on the keyboard: the field stops editing and the keyboard goes (its Esc release is sent); a tap on the field
# brings it back (no hide or show key: F1 rule)
tapkey Esc
shot osk_esc
tapfield Password
shot osk_retap
